{"id":"mahabharata-4-040","work":"mahabharata","part":4,"partName":"विराटपर्व","partNameEn":"Virata Parva","unit":40,"title":"चत्वारिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 40 · Arjuna arms himself","summary":{"en":"Arjuna takes off his bangles, binds his hair, puts on armour, and strings the Gandiva, whose twang strikes the Kurus like a thunderclap. He asks Uttara to drive towards the enemy, and the prince rejoices that his guess was right.","kn":"ಅರ್ಜುನನು ಬಳೆಗಳನ್ನು ತೆಗೆದು ಕೂದಲು ಕಟ್ಟಿ ಕವಚ ತೊಟ್ಟು ಗಾಂಡೀವಕ್ಕೆ ಹೆದೆ ಏರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಅದರ ಟಂಕಾರ ಕುರುಗಳಿಗೆ ಸಿಡಿಲಿನಂತೆ ಕೇಳಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ಶತ್ರುಗಳತ್ತ ರಥ ನಡೆಸೆಂದು ಉತ್ತರನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ತನ್ನ ಊಹೆ ಸರಿಯಾಯಿತೆಂದು ರಾಜಕುಮಾರನು ಹರ್ಷಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"अर्जुन चूड़ियाँ उतारकर बाल बाँधते हैं, कवच पहनते हैं और गाण्डीव पर प्रत्यञ्चा चढ़ाते हैं, जिसकी टंकार कुरुओं को वज्रपात-सी सुनाई देती है। वे उत्तर से शत्रु की ओर रथ ले चलने को कहते हैं, और राजकुमार प्रसन्न होता है कि उसका अनुमान सही निकला।","te":"అర్జునుడు గాజులు తీసి జుట్టు కట్టుకొని కవచం ధరించి గాండీవానికి నారి కడతాడు, దాని టంకారం కురువులకు పిడుగులా వినిపిస్తుంది. శత్రువుల వైపు రథం నడపమని ఉత్తరునికి చెబుతాడు; తన ఊహ నిజమైనందుకు రాజకుమారుడు ఆనందిస్తాడు.","ta":"அர்ஜுனன் வளையல்களைக் கழற்றி முடியைக் கட்டிக் கவசம் அணிந்து காண்டீவத்தில் நாண் ஏற்ற, அதன் ஒலி குருக்களுக்கு இடி முழக்கம் போல் கேட்கிறது. பகைவரை நோக்கித் தேரைச் செலுத்துமாறு உத்தரனிடம் சொல்ல, தன் ஊகம் சரியானதற்கு இளவரசன் மகிழ்கிறான்.","ml":"അർജുനൻ വളകൾ അഴിച്ചുമാറ്റി മുടി കെട്ടി, കവചം ധരിച്ച് ഗാണ്ഡീവത്തിൽ ഞാൺ വലിച്ചുകെട്ടുന്നു; അതിന്റെ മുഴക്കം കുരുക്കളെ ഇടിമുഴക്കംപോലെ ഞെട്ടിക്കുന്നു. ശത്രുവിന് നേരെ രഥം തെളിക്കാൻ അദ്ദേഹം ഉത്തരനോട് ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു; തന്റെ ഊഹം ശരിയായതിൽ രാജകുമാരൻ സന്തോഷിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 4.40; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Dec  1 2011","sections":[{"title":"गोग्रहणपर्व","titleEn":"Gograhana Parva (The cattle raid)","verses":[{"text":"उत्तर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Uttara said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"आस्थाय विपुलं वीर रथं सारथिना मया ।\nकतमं यास्यसेऽनीकमुक्तो यास्याम्यहं त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Hero, mount your great chariot with me as charioteer. Tell me which army you will go to; I will go as you say.\""}},{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"प्रीतोऽस्मि पुरुषव्याघ्र न भयं विद्यते तव ।\nसर्वान्नुदामि ते शत्रून्रणे रणविशारद ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I am pleased, tiger among men; you have nothing to fear. I will drive off all your enemies in battle, skilled one."}},{"n":3,"text":"स्वस्थो भव महाबुद्धे पश्य मां शत्रुभिः सह ।\nयुध्यमानं विमर्देऽस्मिन्कुर्वाणं भैरवं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Be calm, wise one, and watch me fight the enemy in this melee, doing something fearsome and great."}},{"n":4,"text":"एतान्सर्वानुपासङ्गान्क्षिप्रं बध्नीहि मे रथे ।\nएतं चाहर निस्त्रिंशं जातरूपपरिष्कृतम् ।\nअहं वै कुरुभिर्योत्स्याम्यवजेष्यामि ते पशून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Quickly tie all these quivers to my chariot and bring that sword adorned with gold. I will fight the Kurus and win back your cattle."}},{"n":5,"text":"संकल्पपक्षविक्षेपं बाहुप्राकारतोरणम् ।\nत्रिदण्डतूणसंबाधमनेकध्वजसंकुलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Have your chariot's body serve me as a city, with my resolve for ramparts, my arms for walls and gates, three-staffed quivers crowded within, many banners flying,"}},{"n":6,"text":"ज्याक्षेपणं क्रोधकृतं नेमीनिनददुन्दुभि ।\nनगरं ते मया गुप्तं रथोपस्थं भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"with the bowstring's twang for its alarm, anger its builder, and the rumble of the wheel-rims its drum; guarded by me, that will be your city."}},{"n":7,"text":"अधिष्ठितो मया संख्ये रथो गाण्डीवधन्वना ।\nअजेयः शत्रुसैन्यानां वैराटे व्येतु ते भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With me, wielder of the Gandiva, mounted on it, the chariot cannot be defeated by enemy armies. Let your fear go, son of Virata.\""}},{"text":"उत्तर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Uttara said:"}},{"n":8,"text":"बिभेमि नाहमेतेषां जानामि त्वां स्थिरं युधि ।\nकेशवेनापि संग्रामे साक्षादिन्द्रेण वा समम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I am not afraid of them; I know you are steady in battle, equal even to Keshava or to Indra himself."}},{"n":9,"text":"इदं तु चिन्तयन्नेव परिमुह्यामि केवलम् ।\nनिश्चयं चापि दुर्मेधा न गच्छामि कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"But thinking about this, I am only bewildered, and my dull mind cannot reach any conclusion."}},{"n":10,"text":"एवं वीराङ्गरूपस्य लक्षणैरुचितस्य च ।\nकेन कर्मविपाकेन क्लीबत्वमिदमागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one with the body of a hero and fit with such marks, by what ripening of deeds has this unmanliness come?"}},{"n":11,"text":"मन्ये त्वां क्लीबवेषेण चरन्तं शूलपाणिनम् ।\nगन्धर्वराजप्रतिमं देवं वापि शतक्रतुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think you go about in the dress of a eunuch as the trident-bearer Shiva, or a god like the king of the Gandharvas, or Indra himself.\""}},{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"भ्रातुर्नियोगाज्ज्येष्ठस्य संवत्सरमिदं व्रतम् ।\nचरामि ब्रह्मचर्यं वै सत्यमेतद्ब्रवीमि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"By my eldest brother's command I am keeping this vow for a year, living in chastity; I tell you this is true."}},{"n":13,"text":"नास्मि क्लीबो महाबाहो परवान्धर्मसंयुतः ।\nसमाप्तव्रतमुत्तीर्णं विद्धि मां त्वं नृपात्मज ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am not a eunuch, mighty-armed one; I am bound to another and bound to dharma. Know me, prince, as one whose vow is complete and crossed.\""}},{"text":"उत्तर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Uttara said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"परमोऽनुग्रहो मेऽद्य यत्प्रतर्को न मे वृथा ।\nन हीदृशाः क्लीबरूपा भवन्तीह नरोत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"It is a great kindness to me today that my guess was not in vain, for men of such excellence are never really of eunuch form."}},{"n":15,"text":"सहायवानस्मि रणे युध्येयममरैरपि ।\nसाध्वसं तत्प्रनष्टं मे किं करोमि ब्रवीहि मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"With you as helper, I could fight even the immortals; my fear has gone. Tell me what I should do."}},{"n":16,"text":"अहं ते संग्रहीष्यामि हयाञ्शत्रुरथारुजः ।\nशिक्षितो ह्यस्मि सारथ्ये तीर्थतः पुरुषर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will hold your horses, which smash enemy chariots, for I have been properly trained in driving, best of men."}},{"n":17,"text":"दारुको वासुदेवस्य यथा शक्रस्य मातलिः ।\nतथा मां विद्धि सारथ्ये शिक्षितं नरपुंगव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know me, bull among men, as skilled at driving as Daruka for Vasudeva or Matali for Shakra."}},{"n":18,"text":"यस्य याते न पश्यन्ति भूमौ प्राप्तं पदं पदम् ।\nदक्षिणं यो धुरं युक्तः सुग्रीवसदृशो हयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The horse yoked at the right pole, like Sugriva, whose steps are not seen when it runs, touching the ground at each step;"}},{"n":19,"text":"योऽयं धुरं धुर्यवरो वामं वहति शोभनः ।\nतं मन्ये मेघपुष्पस्य जवेन सदृशं हयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"the fine one that draws the left pole, best of yoke horses, I think swift as Meghapushpa."}},{"n":20,"text":"योऽयं काञ्चनसंनाहः पार्ष्णिं वहति शोभनः ।\nवामं सैन्यस्य मन्ये तं जवेन बलवत्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The handsome one in golden mail that bears the rear left side, I think is the strongest in speed for the army's left."}},{"n":21,"text":"योऽयं वहति ते पार्ष्णिं दक्षिणामञ्चितोद्यतः ।\nबलाहकादपि मतः स जवे वीर्यवत्तरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The one bearing your rear right side, head raised and bent, is thought stronger in speed even than Balahaka."}},{"n":22,"text":"त्वामेवायं रथो वोढुं संग्रामेऽर्हति धन्विनम् ।\nत्वं चेमं रथमास्थाय योद्धुमर्हो मतो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"This chariot is fit to carry only you, an archer, in battle, and I think you alone are fit to fight from it.\""}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":23,"text":"ततो निर्मुच्य बाहुभ्यां वलयानि स वीर्यवान् ।\nचित्रे दुन्दुभिसंनादे प्रत्यमुञ्चत्तले शुभे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, removing the bracelets from his arms, the mighty one fastened on the gauntlets of fine make, resounding like a drum, on his beautiful palms."}},{"n":24,"text":"कृष्णान्भङ्गीमतः केशाञ्श्वेतेनोद्ग्रथ्य वाससा ।\nअधिज्यं तरसा कृत्वा गाण्डीवं व्याक्षिपद्धनुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He tied his black, curly hair up with a white cloth, strung the Gandiva quickly and twanged the bow."}},{"n":25,"text":"तस्य विक्षिप्यमाणस्य धनुषोऽभून्महास्वनः ।\nयथा शैलस्य महतः शैलेनैवाभिजघ्नुषः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he flexed it, the bow made a great roar, as if a huge mountain were struck by another mountain."}},{"n":26,"text":"सनिर्घाताभवद्भूमिर्दिक्षु वायुर्ववौ भृशम् ।\nभ्रान्तद्विजं खं तदासीत्प्रकम्पितमहाद्रुमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth seemed to resound with thunderclaps, the wind blew hard in all directions, the sky was full of dazed birds, and great trees trembled."}},{"n":27,"text":"तं शब्दं कुरवोऽजानन्विस्फोटमशनेरिव ।\nयदर्जुनो धनुःश्रेष्ठं बाहुभ्यामाक्षिपद्रथे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Kurus knew that sound as the burst of a thunderbolt, when Arjuna drew the best of bows from his chariot with both arms."}}]}]}